  "verdict": "NO parent-local criterion. Singleton children are always deleted by del_ball. Half of events are 2-sample parents, so n_opp at hd1 equals 1 and hd2 is usually undefined. hd1_norm, n_opp within {1,2,3}\u00b7hd1, sibling purity, and KMeans purity gain all sit near AUROC 0.5 for telling globally class-isolated outliers from lone-in-parent points that still have same-class neighbours outside the parent. The only clean separator is d_same_global / hd1 \u2014 looking outside the parent \u2014 which is the definition of C, not a new local rule. A repair that uses only the parent ball cannot distinguish legitimate isolated minority/boundary points from true outliers.",
  "label_definitions": {
    "A": "parent-local or global minority peeled from a same-class neighbour assigned to the sibling, with d_same_parent <= 2*hd1",
    "C": "no same-class neighbour anywhere in the train set within 2*hd1",
    "B": "neither A nor C, or A/C conflict"
  },
